// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_lolbin_rasautou_dll_execution.yml
// ID Sigma: cd3d1298-eb3b-476c-ac67-12847de55813
// Título: DLL Execution via Rasautou.exe
// Descripción: Detects using Rasautou.exe for loading arbitrary .DLL specified in -d option and executes the export specified in -p.
// Fecha de creación: 2020-10-09
// Fecha de modificación: 
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation | Definición: Since options '-d' and '-p' were removed in Windows 10 this rule is relevant only for Windows before 10. And as Windows 7 doesn't log command line in 4688 by default, to detect this attack you need Sysmon 1 configured or KB3004375 installed for command-line auditing (https://support.microsoft.com/en-au/help/3004375/microsoft-security-advisory-update-to-improve-windows-command-line-aud)
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_lolbin_rasautou_dll_execution.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\rasautou.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "rasdlui.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -d " and ProcessCommandLine contains " -p ")
